  "summary": "Expands the shellcheck linter to check any file containing a shell shebang rather than only files ending in `.sh`. It removes the need to manually append Guix scripts to the check list and drops the global shellcheck exclusion for SC2162 (`read -r`), updating shell scripts to preserve backslash escapes in `read` calls.",
  "problem": "The shellcheck linter silently ignores shell scripts that do not use a `.sh` file extension, requiring manual additions (such as Guix scripts) to maintain coverage. Additionally, the global suppression of SC2162 permits unescaped `read` invocations across shell scripts.",
